From: wilkbook packaging
Subject: build: make BPF compiler and headers explicit

This is a build-environment adaptation, not a gVisor runtime fix.  Bazel's
genrule otherwise invokes a PATH-selected clang and an Ubuntu multiarch
/usr/include directory.  The Guix package supplies both values through the
strict action environment.  Clang's BPF target intentionally has no host CPU
predefine; identify the declared x86-64 libc headers explicitly so glibc does
not select an unavailable 32-bit ABI stub.

--- a/tools/bazeldefs/defs.bzl
+++ b/tools/bazeldefs/defs.bzl
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ def bpf_program(name, src, bpf_object, visibility, hdrs):
     native.genrule(
         name = name,
         srcs = [src],
         visibility = visibility,
         outs = [bpf_object],
-        cmd = "clang -O2 -Wall -Werror -target bpf -c $< -o $@ -I/usr/include/$$(uname -m)-linux-gnu",
+        cmd = "\"$$GVISOR_BPF_CLANG\" -O2 -Wall -Werror -target bpf -D__x86_64__ -c $< -o $@ $$GVISOR_BPF_INCLUDE_FLAGS",
     )
